      ],
      "id": "a18e9166-29ca-4aaf-8da0-7dbc07108d3e",
      "name": "Upload protected document to Drive"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Save the result\n\nGoogle Drive, operation Upload File.\n\nOne protected file per row, named after the employee.\n\nAdd a Gmail node here to mail each person their own document.",
        "height": 557,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1660,
        476
      ],
      "id": "f05e7ee4-c1b8-4e9a-8a8f-dc544f6cff2c",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Upload protected document to Drive"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Password protect a PDF\n\n**Before running:** set your credential on every Cloud Office Print, Google Drive and Google Sheets node, one by one. n8n does not copy credentials across imported nodes. Then pick your own files in the empty File and Document fields.\n\nDownloads a PDF from Drive, sets a read password and a modify password, and uploads the locked file.\n\nThe passwords are hard-coded here to keep the example readable. In a real workflow read them from a sheet as in the flow above, or from an environment variable with `{{ $env.PDF_PASSWORD }}`.\n\n### Setup\nUpload `docs/assets/samples/invoice-2024-001.pdf` to your Drive.",
        "height": 433,
        "width": 1660,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -20,
        1309
      ],
      "id": "27007f10-71ea-4046-8e53-c92c70bb1fbb",
      "name": "Sticky Note - PDF overview"
    },
